  "question": {
    "text": "An ordered pair <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> for which the system of linear equations<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> has a unique solution, is :"
  },
